Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B token embeddings — OLD VOCABULARY (deconfounding table)
============================================================================

READ THIS FIRST: this directory is a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT, not a shipping one.
It exists to separate two variables and is expected to be deleted once that
measurement is recorded. Nothing here is wired into the build, and
`vendored/qwen3/` — not this — is the table the swap ships.

What it is
----------
The same Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B extraction that produced `vendored/qwen3/`, run
over the OLD token list instead of the new one. `code_tokens.txt` here is
byte-identical to `vendored/nomic/code_tokens.txt` (sha256
c928f5e2f9dd85f2294a50a05dd9f2f8bc95192727579aa16b062ff8ef301d25), including
its 11 empty-string entries and their exact positions, so index i names the
same string in both tables.

Why it exists
-------------
The swap moved two levers at once — Track D's revised vocabulary and the model
— and NEXT-STEPS.md section 2 requires the two deltas to be reported
separately. With this table as the middle term:

  nomic + old vocab  ->  THIS (qwen3 + old vocab)   = model-only delta
  THIS               ->  qwen3 + new vocab          = vocabulary-only delta

